			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">The lizard smiles from his seat at the fire and just sips at his cup of coffee his dragon helm sitting beside him as he just listens to the words going around before speaking up, He just waits to measure the weight of the words he is about to speak to those around him.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
The Samurai just chuckles before speak, &quot;now, now m'lord Sarxas. I would have thought that I would have been able to at least have taught you that one should never judge a book before you read it.&quot; The Iksarian turns his head to regard the man with his opalessent eyes, the flames of the hearth dancing in his eyes. &quot;However as much as I might have been enjoying my cup of coffee, I am intregued to hear the story your young friend here speaks of. It is not often I hear of people adventuring so close to those lands that I have been calling home for such a long time now.&quot; He turns his chair around slowly to face the two. &quot;That is... If you would not mind telling your story to an old samurai.&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Rithnok smiles warmly before resting his right ankle on his left knee and resting his right elbow upon his right knee. his eyes telling of the intrigue that crosses his mind at the story of this newcomer.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
